.Dd November 19, 2026
.Dt UPKG 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm upkg
.Nd DER/32 Unix package manager
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl r Ar root
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
installs, removes and upgrades third-party software on DER/32.
Packages come from any number of configured repositories, each published
with an Ed25519-signed index; every package archive is verified against the
SHA-256 digest recorded in that signed index before anything is installed.
Packages install below
.Pa /usr/local
by default; the base system is never modified by
.Nm .
.Pp
The global options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl r Ar root
Operate on the system rooted at
.Ar root
instead of
.Pa / .
Configuration, the database and the installed files are all taken relative
to
.Ar root .
.It Fl v
Print debugging output.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm sync
Download every enabled repository's
.Pa INDEX
and
.Pa INDEX.sig ,
verify the signature against the trusted keys in
.Pa /etc/upkg/keys ,
and refuse indexes that name a different repository or are older than the
copy already held.
.It Cm install Oo Fl n Oc Oo Fl Fl asdeps Oc Oo Fl Fl nodeps Oc Oo Fl Fl allow-unsigned Oc Ar package ...
Install packages and their dependencies.
A
.Ar package
is
.Ar name ,
.Ar repo Ns / Ns Ar name
(take it from that repository only),
.Ar name Ns Op <,<=,=,>=,> Ns Ar version
or the path of a local
.Pa .upkg
file
(which requires
.Fl Fl allow-unsigned ) .
.Fl n
only prints the transaction.
.It Cm remove Oo Fl n Oc Oo Fl c Oc Ar package ...
Remove packages.
Removal of a package another package depends on is refused unless
.Fl c
is given, in which case the dependents are removed as well.
.It Cm autoremove Op Fl n
Remove packages that were installed only as dependencies and are no longer
required.
.It Cm upgrade Op Fl n
Upgrade every installed package for which a repository offers a newer
version.
.It Cm search Ar query
Search package names and descriptions.
.It Cm info Ar package
Show installed and repository information.
.It Cm list Oo Fl e | Fl d Oc Op Fl f Ar package
List installed packages
.Pq Fl e : No explicitly installed only, Fl d : No dependencies only ,
or the files owned by
.Ar package .
.It Cm check Op Ar package ...
Verify installed files against the checksums in the database.
.It Cm build Oo Fl o Ar output Oc Ar port
Build a package from the source recipe
.Ar port
(a directory, or a name looked up in
.Ar portsdir ) .
When run as root the build runs as the unprivileged
.Ar build_user .
Recipes are only ever executed on explicit request.
.It Cm repo list | add Ar name url Oo Fl p Ar prio Oc Oo Fl k Ar key Oc Oo Fl Fl disabled Oc | remove Ar name | enable Ar name | disable Ar name | priority Ar name n
Manage repositories.
.It Cm keygen Ar prefix
Create
.Ar prefix Ns .key
and
.Ar prefix Ns .pub .
.It Cm create Fl i Ar PKGINFO Fl d Ar stagedir Op Fl o Ar file
Create a package from a staging directory.
.It Cm index Fl n Ar repo Fl k Ar keyfile Ar dir
Write and sign
.Ar dir Ns /INDEX .
.It Cm recover
Complete or undo an interrupted transaction.
This also happens automatically before any command that modifies the system.
.It Cm vercmp Ar a b
Print \-1, 0 or 1.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/upkg/repos.conf -compact
.It Pa /etc/upkg/upkg.conf
options:
.Cm arch , prefixes , portsdir , builddir , build_user , ca_file , allow_http
.It Pa /etc/upkg/repos.conf
repositories:
.Cm url , priority , enabled , key
.It Pa /etc/upkg/keys/
trusted Ed25519 public keys
.It Pa /var/lib/upkg/upkg.db
installed package database
.It Pa /var/lib/upkg/journal
transaction journal
.It Pa /var/cache/upkg/
downloaded packages and distfiles
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# upkg repo add core https://example.org/der32/core -p 100
# upkg sync
# upkg install core/curl
# upkg remove curl && upkg autoremove
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pkg_add 1 ,
.Xr hier 7
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in DER/32 0.1
.Dq Genesis .
